# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/

# Application workspace state (Freebuff client) — not project content
.freebuff/

# Generated AF3 job files / export trees (regenerate with `configbuilder`)
# — root-anchored so it never matches the configbuilder/output source package
/output/

# Internal working copies (.cbproj autosave) — the application's resume state
.configbuilder/

# OS and editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large local reference data — kept out of the repository on purpose.
#
# `testdata/` holds two multi-megabyte MSA JSON dumps (23.4 MB and 12.0 MB).
# No test, fixture or runtime module reads them: they are reference examples of
# the protein/RNA/ligand MSA shapes, recorded in HANDOFF.md as "referenced by
# no current test". They stay on disk and out of Git so a clone stays small.
# Root-anchored: nothing under tests/fixtures/ is affected by this rule.
/testdata/

# The three planning documents below describe how the project was built rather
# than what it ships, and they are read by nothing — no test, fixture or runtime
# module. They stay on disk and untracked by decision, not by accident.
#
# `AUTHORITATIVE_SPEC.md` and `DOMAIN_MAPPING.md` are deliberately NOT here:
# `tests/contract/test_catalogue_traceability.py` reads both files and fails
# collection without them, so a clone that omitted them could not run the suite
# at all. They are the contract this builder's rule catalogue is transcribed
# from, i.e. test input, not commentary.
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
HANDOFF.md
CHECKLIST.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verification material: kept on disk, deliberately untracked.
#
# The builder was verified locally; the repository now carries the application
# and launchers only. These files remain in the working copy so they can still
# be read or run, but they are not part of Git and no clone needs them.
#
#   tests/       the local test suite and its fixtures
#   docs/        local reports, prompts and reference material
#   .github/    local CI configuration
#   *.md         root specifications, audits and READMEs
#
tests/
docs/
.github/
*.md
